<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Louis Rwagasore</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1932–1961</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Prince Louis Rwagasore</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Prince Louis Rwagasore was a Burundian nationalist, son of Mwami <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mwambutsa-iv">Mwambutsa IV</a>, who led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/union-for-national-progress">UPRONA</a> party to victory in the elections of September 1961. He became prime minister but was assassinated in October 1961 by a Greek gunman hired by politicians of a rival party. He is honoured as Burundi's national hero of independence.</p></div>
